application program interface (API) and subject to relevant terms of use. There is no required hardware or software to use the model. For AI Studio and Gemini API, see the 【65†Gemini API Additional Terms of Service†ai.google.dev】; for Gemini for business, see 【66†Google Cloud Platform Terms of Service†cloud.google.com】. For more information, see 【67†Gemini Model API instructions†ai.google.dev】 and 【68†Gemini API quickstart†ai.google.dev】.\nL178: \nL179: * * *\nL180: ## Evaluation\nL181: \nL182: ### Approach\nL183: \nL184: Gemini 4 Argon was evaluated across a range of benchmarks, including agentic coding, ML engineering, computer use, knowledge work, science and math, multimodal capabilities, long-context and cybersecurity. Additional benchmarks and details on approach, results and their methodologies can be found at: 【69†deepmind.com/models/evals-methodology/gemini-4-argon†deepmind.com】.\nL185: ### Results\nL186: \nL187: Gemini 4 Argon results as of October, 2026 are below:\nL188: Category  | Benchmark  | Notes  | Gemini 4 Argon  | GPT-6 Astra  | Claude Fable 5.1  | Claude Opus 5.5\nL189: --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nL190: Knowledge work  | Vals Index  |  | 68.9%  | 63.1%  | 65.8%  | 67.0%\nL191: AutomationBench  | Score  | 51.3%  | 41.4%  | 31.4%  | 42.5%\nL192: Vals Finance Agent v2  |  | 65.4%  | 53.5%  | 58.9%  | 58.6%\nL193: Harvey's Legal Agent Benchmark  |  | 19.6%  | 5.4%  | 6.7%  | 3.8%\nL194: Agentic coding  | DeepSWE v1.1  |  | 77.9%  | 74.1%  | 67.4%  | 74.2%\nL195: FrontierSWE v2  |  | 55.0%  | 65.5%  | 56.3%  | 62.3%\nL196: Vibe Code Bench  |  | 91.9%  | 89.6%  | 90.3%  | 90.3%\nL197: Terminal-bench 4.0  |  | 57.4%  | 58.2%  | 57.9%  | 66.4%\nL198: ML engineering  | PostTrainBench  |  | 45.3%  | 44.3%  | 40.2%  | 49.3%\nL199: Science and math  | Terminal-Bench Science 0.1  |  | 57.6%  | 68.1%  | 52.6%  | 63.3%\nL200: LABBench 2  |  | 88.8%  | 85.4%  | 68.6%  | 73.1%\nL201: RiemannBench  |  | 76.0%  | 72.0%  | 65.6%  | 69.6%\nL202: Long context  | GraphWalks  | Up to 128k, BFS (F1)  | 99.7%  | 98.7%  | 91.4%  | 90.6%\nL203: 256k to 1M, BFS (F1)  | 84.2%  | 71.8%  | 65.0%  | 66.8%\nL204: Computer use  | Agent's Last Exam  | Pass rate  | 39.5%  | 34.2%  | —  | 38.2%\nL205: OSWorld-2.0  | Offline subset\nL206: Partial score  | 69.2%  | 72.6%  | —  | —\nL207: Multimodal understanding  | Chartography  |  | 71.6%  | 71.0%  | 46.2%  | 66.3%\nL208: LVBench  |  | 91.7%  | 87.5%  | 79.7%  | 83.7%\nL209: Cybersecurity  | CWE-bench v1  |  | 68.0%  | 68.0%  | 58.0%  | 67.0%\nL210: Methodology: 【70†deepmind.google/models/evals-methodology/gemini-4-argon】\nL211: ## Intended Usage and Limitations\nL212: ### Benefit and Intended Usage\nL213: \nL214: Gemini 4 Argon is our latest frontier model, excels at deep work in complex, real-world tasks across domains including coding, finance, legal, cybersecurity, and science.\nL215: \nL216: Argon combines frontier reasoning, deep visual perception, expanded domain knowledge, and stronger writing capabilities to help with technical and enterprise workflows.\nL217: \nL218: It is particularly well-suited for applications that require:\nL219:   * multi-turn deep investigations\nL220:   * complex engineering tasks\nL221:   * deep visual understanding\nL222:   * cybersecurity defense\nL223:   * multimodal document analysis and synthesis\nL224:   * deep domain knowledge and strong writing capabilities (e.g. legal and financial analysis, science)\nL225:   * scientific or mathematical reasoning\nL226: ### Known Limitations\nL227: \nL228: Gemini 4 Argon may exhibit some of the general limitations of foundation models, such as hallucinations. There may also be occasional slowness or timeout issues. The knowledge cutoff for Gemini 4 is March 2026, but in some domains the model’s knowledge may be less up to date.\nL229: ### Acceptable Usage\nL230: 【71†Google’s Generative AI Prohibited Use Policy†policies.google.com】 applies to uses of the model in accordance with the applicable terms of service.\nL231: Additionally, the model should not be integrated into certain systems (also found in 【71†Google’s Generative AI Prohibited Use Policy†policies.google.com】), including those that: (1) engage in dangerous or illicit activities, or otherwise violate applicable laws or regulations, (2) compromise the security of others’ or Google’s services, (3) engage in sexually explicit, violent, hateful, or harmful activities, (4) engage in misinformation, misrepresentation, or misleading activities.\n"
